<title>UK: UK output prices unchanged in August.</title>
<headline>UK output prices unchanged in August.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics (ONS) released the following provisional data on UK input and output prices in August (previously announced data in brackets)</p>
<p>    OUTPUT PRICES (unadj) AUGUST   JULY  (PREL JULY)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	  unch    -0.2    (-0.1)</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change	    2.0*     2.2     (2.2)</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)     123.5    123.5 (123.5)</p>
<p>OUTPUT PRICES EX FOOD/DRINK/TOBACCO PETROLEUM (unadj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	  unch    -0.2    (-0.1)</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change	    1.2**    1.4     (1.5)</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)     119.7    119.7 (119.8)</p>
<p>OUTPUT PRICES EX FOOD,DRINK,TOBACCO,PETROLEUM (adj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	  unch    -0.1    (-0.1)</p>
<p>    Yr/Yr change	    1.3	1.5     (1.5)</p>
<p>    Qtr/qtr change	  0.1	0.1     (0.1)</p>
<p>    Qtr/Qtr annual rate   0.2	0.6     (0.6)</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)     119.8    119.8 (119.8)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES (MATERIALS AND FUEL) (unadj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	 -0.3     -0.8    (-0.8)</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change	   -2.1     -2.3    (-2.2)</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)     111.5    111.8 (111.9)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES (MATERIALS AND FUEL) (adj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	  0.3	0.2     (0.3)</p>
<p>    Yr/Yr change	   -2.2     -2.3    (-2.2)</p>
<p>    Index		     113.2    112.9 (113.0)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES EX F,D,T,P (unadj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	  unch    -1.1    (-1.0)</p>
<p>    Yr/Yr change	   -6.6     -6.8    (-6.7)</p>
<p>    Index		     107.1    107.1  (107.2)</p>
<p>INPUT PRICES EX F,D,T,P (adj)</p>
<p>    Monthly change	  0.1     -0.8    (-0.8)</p>
<p>    Yr/Yr  change	  -6.6     -6.7    (-6.6)</p>
<p>    Index		     108.2    108.1  (108.2)</p>
<p>    INPUT COMPONENTS PCT CHANGE    AUG M/M     AUG Y/Y</p>
<p>    fuel				    -0.3	 -5.4</p>
<p>    crude oil etc			  3.5	  28.4</p>
<p>    metals				   0.9	 -13.3</p>
<p>    chemicals			     -0.2	 -6.2</p>
<p>    materials: home produced	  -1.9	  3.2</p>
<p>		   imported		 -0.6	  1.3</p>
<p>    other home produced		  unch	 1.8</p>
<p>    Other imported materials	  -0.8	 -6.9</p>
<p>Consensus of economists' forecasts was for input prices to rise a seasonally adjusted 0.3 percent and fall 2.2 percent year-on-year. Output prices forecast flat on the month, +2.0 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>* The lowest rate of increase since July 1994</p>
<p>** The lowest rate of increase since October 1967.</p>
<p>The ONS said a rise in the price of crude oil was more than offset in input prices by falls in the prices of rubber, paper and seasonal food inputs.</p>
